---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import TextPage from '../components/TextPage.astro';

// TODO before launch: name the operating legal entity and the governing jurisdiction,
// and add shop/purchase terms once the store opens. Have a lawyer review.
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of use — KAVOVO"
  description="The terms that apply when you use the KAVOVO website."
>
  <TextPage
    eyebrow="Terms"
    title="Terms of use"
    intro="What you can expect from this site, and what we ask in return."
    updated="2026-08-05"
  >
    <h2>Using the site</h2>
    <p>
      KAVOVO is free to read. You may use our recipes at home, share links to any page, and quote short passages with
      attribution and a link back.
    </p>

    <h2>What you may not do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Republish whole recipes, guides or articles as your own content.</li>
      <li>Use our photography or the KAVOVO name and logo without written permission.</li>
      <li>Scrape the site at a rate that degrades it for other readers.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Accuracy</h2>
    <p>
      We test recipes before publishing and correct them when readers report problems. Even so, results depend on your
      equipment, water and beans, so we cannot guarantee a particular outcome. Recipes involve hot water, hot milk and
      pressurised equipment — follow your equipment manufacturer's safety instructions.
    </p>

    <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
    <p>
      Where we link to other websites, we do so because we found them useful. We do not control them and are not
      responsible for their content.
    </p>

    <h2>The shop</h2>
    <p>
      Coffee sales have not launched. When they do, purchases will be covered by separate sales terms, published before
      the first order is accepted.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>We may update these terms; the date at the top always shows the current version.</p>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>
      Anything unclear here, ask us at <a href="mailto:hello@kavovo.coffee">hello@kavovo.coffee</a>.
    </p>
  </TextPage>
</Layout>
